  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.639 acc, and the key architectural choices (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) are well-supported. The main untested lever for improvement is the image encoder: ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet should provide substantially richer visual representations than ResNet50. This experiment (config_051: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates the image encoder upgrade while keeping all other proven settings fixed, directly testing whether a stronger visual backbone can push accuracy beyond 0.639. It is the best use of experiment 5 because it exploits the strongest known architecture while probing the single most impactful untested component (image encoder quality). Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high, likely ~15-25 GPU hours (ViT-L is larger than ResNet50, but avgpool+weighted keeps aggregation/fusion overhead low, similar in structure to config_003's 10.60 hrs). This is well within remaining budget and justified by the expected accuracy gain."
}

